Subject: [PATCH 09/11] feat(pqc-m9): structured PQC log with redaction at the
 emit boundary

PQC migration (whitepaper 2.2.9): every PQC event flows through a
single `pqcLog.{info,warn,error,debug}` chokepoint. The emit
boundary applies a uniform redaction pass so subscribers (real loggers
or test recorders) only ever see safe data.

- src/logging/pqc-log.ts:
  - PQC_EVENT vocabulary (wrap-secret, unwrap-secret, device-identity,
    keyring, rotation, backup, restore, doctor) - exported as a
    readonly tuple so a downstream consumer can derive the union type.
  - PqcLogPayload typed shape with optional identityKey, keyId, detail,
    and free-form aux fields. The extra fields flow through redaction.
  - redactPqcLogPayload drops undefined values, drops Buffer / TypedArray
    values, replaces any key matching /passphrase/i, /raw[-_]?key/i,
    /private[-_]?key/i, /secret/i with a [REDACTED] marker, and
    recursively redacts nested plain objects and arrays.
  - setPqcEmit / getPqcEmit / resetPqcEmit are the in-process swap
    surface. bindOpenClawLogger routes the redacted record to the
    appropriate sink (info / warn / error / debug) and tags it with
    `{ tag: "PQC" }` for downstream filtering.
  - pqcLog chokepoint is a stable object reference so M4 and M5 can
    import it without re-creating a closure per call.
- src/logging/pqc-log.test.ts: 10 invariants - PQC_EVENT membership,
  secret-name redaction (case-insensitive, all 4 patterns), Buffer /
  TypedArray drop, undefined drop, nested-object / nested-array
  recursion, chokepoint routing through the swapped emitter,
  bindOpenClawLogger level routing, default-emitter console fallback,
  Buffer-drop inside arrays, and emitter swap identity.

10/10 green.

